      "body": "The new rejection rule is hard to implement as written because the spec doesn’t define what constitutes a “numbered stable R4G1 version” vs a draft version. Since the header already has `format_version (major, minor)`, it would be clearer to make the pre-freeze rule explicitly about reserved version numbers (e.g., major>=1 only after packed widths are frozen), so draft readers/writers can deterministically accept/reject artifacts.",
